aes128cfb is not an HMAC algorithm, but an encryption algorithm.
... and 99% of (physical) TPMs don't support aes128-block-encryption.

I think you'd need -G hmac or -G keyhash or -G sha256 or something similar =
for this.
I don't know the code enough.

Also I don't think it's currently supported, since the flags for -G are asy=
m and sym, but
not hmac or keydhash. (https://github.com/tpm2-software/tpm2-tools/blob/mas=
ter/tools/tpm2_import.c)

Maybe start loking yourself.
If you go through the calltrace from -G you'll end up here for aes:
https://github.com/tpm2-software/tpm2-tools/blob/7ed4cba2918adf6e8bdbbe32fa=
54910e80d53e27/lib/tpm2_openssl.c#L803
We'll need something similar for keyedHash objects of type SHA256 or SHA1...

